From f764f6978a7a9b80a209c2e4f1506631287c2ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:37:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] make the map, the cards and the details one flow, on real
 contact data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two buttons in this app were labelled for work they did not do:

  handleMapProjectSelect(id)  ->  setViewMode("table")
                                  toast.info("Projekt #id in der Tabelle
                                  angezeigt")
  "Details anzeigen"          ->  setViewMode("table")

Nothing was selected, filtered, scrolled to or shown. The toast was the
only evidence anything had happened, and it was false.

Now: a marker's popup offers the station as a whole and each project in
it. Clicking a project switches to the card view, narrows it to that
station's exact project ids (the map passes the ids, so it is an id
match and not a substring of the station name), scrolls the card into
view, rings it for 2.6s and opens its detail dialog. A dismissible
"Station: X" chip says what is being filtered, and the result count
reports what the card view is actually showing rather than the unfiltered
total.

The dialog carries Stammdaten, the Kommentar, all 14 Fachprüfungen with
status tone / Prüfer / Prüfdatum, the per-project audit trail, and a
contact route for each party. Reachable from the cards, the table and
the map, so the three views expose the same action.

shared/contact-resolution.ts — the join, and what it can honestly reach
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hilfsdatei holds full names; the review rows hold surnames. Matching in
full found 1 of 44 reviewer names (32 of 10,489 rows). Matching the
surname is safe here because all 48 Hilfsdatei surnames are unique —
measured, asserted, and enforced: SURNAME_INDEX drops any surname that
ever collides, so a future duplicate degrades to "ambiguous" rather than
addressing mail to the wrong person.

  exact                29 names / 6,855 rows resolve to a real address
  + unique surname
  placeholder           3 names / 2,799 rows are not people at all
                        ("Zuordnung erforderlich", "Zentrale", "BSB des
                        BM´s") and get no mail button
  unknown              12 names /   835 rows have no address on file

That answers the open Stage 4a question with data: the reviewer gap is
11 people and 829 rows (plus "Herr", 6 rows, which is a truncation), not
the 20 people and 1,083 rows that counting full names suggested.

Reach per party, stated in the UI rather than implied by a uniform row
of buttons:

  Bahnhofsmanagement   8 of 8 regions   always contactable
  Fachprüfer          29 of 44 names    else the Fachbereich's own
                                        recipients, else "keine Adresse"
  Projektleiter        3 of 252 names   else the zuständiges BM

No address is ever constructed. `vorname.nachname@deutschebahn.com`
would look right often enough to be dangerous, so `unknown` stays
`unknown`. Teams links are derived from the address already on file, so
the chat and the mail reach the same person. There is no telephone
button because no source carries a telephone number — Hilfsdatei has
columns A-C only — and the dialog says so once instead of rendering a
dead control.

projektLink is rendered as a button only when it parses as an http(s)
URL: 138 of 1,298 rows are populated and 72 of those are free-text
notes, which would have been 72 buttons that navigate nowhere.

Also fixed along the way
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Filter chips dismissed via a bare <X> with an onClick: not focusable,
  no role, not in the tab order. Five filters could be applied by
  keyboard and none removed. Now a real <button> with an aria-label.
- The dialog close button measured 16x44 on every touch device: the
  coarse-pointer rule matched `svg:only-child`, and that button also
  carries a visually hidden label. Now matches "only text is sr-only"
  too — every icon button in the app, not just this one.
- That button's screen-reader label was the English "Close".
- DialogContent ends its class list with `sm:max-w-lg`, so an unprefixed
  `max-w-3xl` never won: the dialog measured 512px wide.
- e2e-smoke treated a failed OpenStreetMap tile as an app defect, so any
  assertion that opened the map failed without egress. Now only
  same-origin console errors fail the suite.

Six new e2e assertions follow the whole path — marker to popup to
filtered cards to dialog to contact link — including one that reads
every mailto: and Teams href out of the dialog and fails if any address
is absent from data/contacts.source.json.

Gates: 0 type errors · 145 passed / 6 skipped (13 files) · lint at
parity with baseline · e2e 28/28 · responsive 61/61 · map chrome 6/6 ·
dialog fits, scrolls and clears 44px on iPhone SE and iPad Pro.
